~ Block-scope join (see docs/concurrency/README.md): a `< >` block joins every launch it
~ made directly before it returns, including one bound to a name it never reads again.
~ `hearsay` is launched and never read; `testimony` is what the block needs.

<< core.io

^ = () -> Num => <
  hearsay = @readStdin()          ~ launched — the block joins it even though it goes unread
  testimony = @readStdin()
  assert(testimony, equals(""))   ~ end-of-input; forces `testimony` (the join settles `hearsay` too)
  0
>
